  "ticket_id": "TP-TICKET-251",
  "theorem_name": "RightEvenModuloEightConstraintAndSharpness",
  "declared_proposition": "For odd primes p,r and integers k,m>=1, if p^k+2=r^(2m), then k is odd and p=7 modulo 8. Conversely, every odd k and odd p=7 modulo 8 satisfies p^k+2=1 modulo 8, so modulo eight alone cannot force k=1 or exclude composite left powers.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Every odd square is 1 modulo 8. If k is even, then p^k=1 modulo 8 and p^k+2=3 modulo 8, impossible. Hence k is odd; for an odd exponent p^k=p modulo 8, so p+2=1 modulo 8 and p=7 modulo 8. Conversely, if k is odd and p=7 modulo 8, then p^k+2=1 modulo 8. This last congruence supplies compatibility only, not an integer solution, and proves the asserted sharp limitation of this route.",
  "result_classification": "partial_theorem",
  "problem_status": "open_not_proven",
